# ISALWA AI Constitution

This repo is in **PRODUCT MATURITY**. Optimize for consistency, maintainability, and enterprise quality. This constitution outranks implementation convenience.

## Core principles

1. Never rewrite working systems.
2. Never create parallel implementations.
3. Extend before replacing.
4. Reuse before creating.
5. Every UI element belongs to the design system (`@isalwa/ui` + tokens).
6. Business logic wins over aesthetics.
7. Architecture stability > visual novelty.
8. Prefer smaller PRs over large refactors.
9. New features must feel like they always existed.
10. If unsure, preserve existing behavior.

## Frozen design language

Porcelain backgrounds · kiln sidebar · glaze accents · Newsreader italic titles · uppercase kickers · 8px rhythm · soft elevation · calm motion · premium enterprise feel.

Do **not** introduce another visual language. Tokens: `packages/ui/src/tokens/tokens.css`. Spec: `docs/design/MISSION11_*.md`, `docs/design/MISSION12_*.md`. Full text: `docs/architecture/AI_CONSTITUTION.md`.

## Never / Always

**Never:** replace frameworks, migrate stacks, competing component systems, duplicate primitives, move business logic without approval, add deps without justification.

**Always:** extend `@isalwa/ui`, reuse primitives, document ADRs when needed, compose over duplicate.

## Before creating a component

Search first: `MetricCard`, `Panel`, `ExperienceHeader`, `Chip`, `Button`, `Timeline`, `SectionHeader`, `InsightCard`, `DashboardGrid`, `ActionBar`, `SearchField`, `PageContainer`, `PageSection`, `StatGroup`, `ListRow`, `EmptyPanel`, `StatusPill`, `EmptyState`.

If it exists → **reuse**. Do not build another.

## Definition of done

Consistent UI · mobile works · a11y preserved · no duplicated components · no dead code · docs updated · types pass · build passes · behavior unchanged.
